4. DATABASE BACKENDS AND CONFIG DEFAULTS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
- QDBM has no real transactions: dddb_txn_begin/commit/abort are stubbed
  (return 0). A kill or ENOSPC during dirty writeback can leave the index or
  chunk inconsistent. Ops: keep flat-dump discipline, monitor disk, and see
  README.DBISCORRUPT. MDBX is the transactional backend.

- fork_dump: default 0 (off). The forked-dump path exists; on non-MDBX
  (QDBM) backends it historically risks corruption. Keep it off unless you
  know why you need it. Under MDBX the fork child opens its own read
  transaction, which is the supported configuration.

- Dual config defaults: cf_init() carries the historical built-in defaults
  (e.g. port 6250), while netrhost.conf / alternate_netrhost.conf overlay
  recommended values (e.g. port 4201). This is 27+ years of compatibility -
  do not unify the layers. When stating "the default is X", say which layer
  you mean.